@@host: Andersen was asked to write a story to go with a picture: a poor child with a bundle of matches. He remembered his own mother, sent out to beg as a girl, who had sat under a bridge all day and cried.

@@host: The story is very short and very sad. In the morning, the people who find her say she wanted to warm herself. Nobody knows what she saw.

